2. Technical Architecture
2.1 Orchestration Pattern Choice
Recommended pattern for v1

Do not start with full multi-agent autonomy.
AI Agent Orchestration Patterns - Azure Architecture Center says architects should use the lowest level of complexity that reliably meets requirements, because each level of agent architecture introduces coordination overhead, latency, and cost. It also says a single agent with tools is often the right default for enterprise use cases and is simpler to debug and test than multiagent setups. [learn.microsoft.com]
Why not full multi-agent in v1?
Multiagent orchestration is useful when a single agent cannot reliably handle the problem due to prompt complexity, tool overload, or security requirements, but it adds coordination overhead, latency, and failure modes. [learn.microsoft.com]
So v1 should be:
Plain Text1Controlled Orchestrator2Specialized internal tools3Strict policy engine4No autonomous production changes5`Show more lines
Future versions can introduce specialized agents.

